From: Son Luong Ngoc <26684313+sluongng@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 19:56:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] jj: Merge prepared read-only indexes

A custom index can prepare a complete immutable remote checkpoint
without constructing another ReadonlyRepo. Importing that checkpoint
before loading selected commits lets the repository use exact index
membership instead of walking their public ancestry.

Expose a narrow read-only-index merge entry point and delegate the
existing repository-based helper to it. Compatibility checks remain
with the index backend. This does not expose mutable index internals,
admit objects or change repository views and references.

---
diff --git a/src/repo.rs b/src/repo.rs
--- a/src/repo.rs
+++ b/src/repo.rs
@@ -2057,7 +2057,16 @@
     }
 
     pub fn merge_index(&mut self, other_repo: &ReadonlyRepo) -> IndexResult<()> {
-        self.index.merge_in(other_repo.readonly_index())
+        self.merge_index_from(other_repo.readonly_index())
+    }
+
+    /// Merges an already prepared read-only index without changing the view.
+    ///
+    /// Index backends can use this to import an immutable remote checkpoint
+    /// before loading its selected commits. The index implementation checks
+    /// compatibility; this method does not admit objects or update references.
+    pub fn merge_index_from(&mut self, other_index: &dyn ReadonlyIndex) -> IndexResult<()> {
+        self.index.merge_in(other_index)
     }
 
     async fn merge_view(&mut self, base: &View, other: &View) -> Result<(), RepoLoaderError> {
